<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="218c" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Package scope by rule (every sprk component in the authoring environment + OOB columns − committed exclusions), two-way drift check, and an export step that writes SpaarkeMaster as unpacked source into git with no environment-variable values</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T218 (D7, G11); notes/t218-plan.md design 2, 3, 7</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Release tooling that decides what every customer receives; PowerShell + tests; reads the dev environment.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The scope rule is the package definition; a wrong rule ships a customer without the Console (F7).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>scripts/ and docs/data-model only.</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, dataverse, solution, scripts, testing</tags>
    <deps>218a</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make "what ships" a rule that cannot silently miss a component, and make each release a reviewable diff in git.</prompt>

  <goal>
    `Get-SpaarkeComponents.ps1` enumerates every unmanaged `sprk`-prefixed component in the authoring environment
    (tables, columns, option sets, relationships, forms, views, web resources, PCF controls, roles, app modules, site maps,
    environment-variable definitions) plus the OOB columns in oob-customizations.yaml, minus
    `docs/data-model/package-scope.json` (each entry has a reason and a date). `Test-SolutionCompleteness.ps1` fails when a
    component matches the rule but is not in SpaarkeMaster, and when a SpaarkeMaster component is gone from dev.
    `Export-SpaarkeMasterSource.ps1` exports SpaarkeMaster managed + unmanaged from dev, unpacks both into
    `src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/`, and removes environment-variable values; a test fails if values appear.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>t218-plan.md F6, F7, F10: membership-based scope misses code pages created in the Default solution
      (sprk_spaarkeai, sprk_dailyupdate checked 2026-10-07); the 2026-08-21 package carried dev env-var values.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>scripts/solution-authoring/{Get-SpaarkeComponents,Assemble-SpaarkeMasterSolution,Test-SolutionCompleteness}.ps1</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/{spaarke-components-inventory.json,oob-customizations.yaml}; scripts/Build-SpaarkeMaster.ps1 (exclusions 73-85, values 295-306)</file>
      <file>src/dataverse/solutions/ (spaarke_core, spaarke_documents .gitkeep only; spaarke_containers)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/t218-plan.md</file>
      <file>docs/procedures/SPAARKE-SOLUTION-RELEASE-PROCESS.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="live">Reading dev (Web API GET, pac solution export) is allowed. Adding components to SpaarkeMaster in dev (Assemble without -WhatIf) is a live change — ask the owner first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="exclusions">Seed the exclusions file from the 2026-08-21 owner-directed PCF exclusions, the test/scratch pattern and sprk_SpaarkePlatform — each with its reason and date; nothing excluded silently in code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no values">No environment-variable values (component type 381 / environmentvariablevalues.json) in source or in a packed zip.</constraint>
    <constraint source="reuse">Extend the three existing scripts; Build-SpaarkeMaster.ps1 retires if Assemble + Export cover it (grep callers first).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Scope rule in Get-SpaarkeComponents (prefix + type queries, not solution membership) + exclusions file; inventory JSON gains name + type per component.</step>
    <step order="2">Two-way drift in Test-SolutionCompleteness against SpaarkeMaster's actual membership; -WhatIf report of what Assemble would add (read-only run against dev, report attached to notes).</step>
    <step order="3">Export-SpaarkeMasterSource.ps1 (export both, `pac solution unpack --packagetype Both`, strip values, deterministic output); value guard test (Pester or a ControlPlane/ArchTests file test).</step>
    <step order="4">Retire Build-SpaarkeMaster.ps1 if unused; runbook steps updated; verify; Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Against dev (read-only), the drift report lists the in-scope components SpaarkeMaster lacks (proves the rule catches what membership missed). [Amended 2026-10-07: the original wording named sprk_spaarkeai/sprk_dailyupdate on a wrong premise — both are in SpaarkeMaster.]</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An excluded component never appears as drift; a component excluded without a reason fails validation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The value guard fails on a fixture containing environmentvariablevalues.json and passes on the stripped tree.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Export script -WhatIf/dry run prints the export + unpack commands without writing to dev.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes/>
</task>
